                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any single-celled green alga, of the genus Chlorella, found especially in stagnant water; now produced commercially as a food supplement."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "174524f5-8eb1-4ba2-8f8b-c5f9c0ee4e04",
                                                "sense_id": "d417bb68-802f-335e-a5a8-d777f2a87170",
                                                "text": "Many people use chlorella for a nutrient factor isolated in the 1950s and not available in other green foods: \"Chlorella Growth Factor\" (CGF). CGF is related to the special nature of chlorella's nucleic acid. The nucleic acid in the human body ..."
